BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-i.MX8MP-PD24.1.2    2024-06-26
=================================================
- Linux Kernel v6.6.21-phy1
- U-boot v2024.01-phy4
- Yocto Scarthgap (5.0.1)
- Qt 6.6.3
- RAUC 1.11.3

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt6demo-image:
  * phyboard-pollux-imx8mp-3

- phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-pollux-imx8mp-3

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04 64-bit

Issues fixed:
-------------

New Features:
-------------
- Add support for 1GB, 4GB and 8GB RAM
- Add support for 1.5GHz and 2GHz RAM timings where supported by hardware
- Default to compressed generated OS Images via Yocto (wic.xz)

Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
- When using UUU, the flash target for an OS image must be hard-coded in U-Boot
  Kconfig to either eMMC or SD card. By default, it is set to eMMC. This means
  that flashing an OS image to SD card via the built-in UUU script sd_all will
  instead flash the eMMC device. U-Boot sources must be altered and thus
  recompiled to change this behaviour.
- When setting the backlight brightness to "1" for the AC200 display, the light
  will flicker.
- The largest continuous main memory area available in U-Boot is about 1.28 GB.
  This means that, when flashing an OS image via U-Boot, the image must be
  smaller than 1.28 GB.


