=================================================
- Linux Kernel v6.6.21-phy1
- U-boot v2024.01-phy3
- Yocto Scarthgap development state (pre 5.0)
- Qt 6.6.3
- RAUC 1.11.3

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt6demo-image:
  * phyboard-pollux-imx8mp-3

- phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-pollux-imx8mp-3

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04 64-bit

Features:
---------
Feature set is limited in comparison to the PD23.1.0 release.
As this BSP is based on upstream kernel/u-boot and not based on an NXP BSP.

All features included in this release are also upstream available.

- Supporting 2GB RAM only (1,5GHz and 2GHz depending on the SoM revision)
- eMMC/SD-Card/serial downloader/network boot support
- ethernet support
- thermal support
- SPI NOR flash (no boot support)
- GPU support
- CPU frequency scaling
- RAUC update support
- USB support
- LVDS1
- CAN
- UART/RS485
- watchdog
- RTC
- PWM
- Wayland/Weston
- QT6
- Video decoding (software only)

Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
- Release Manifest does not point to correct branch of meta-phytec,
  meta-ampliphy and meta-qt6-phytec.
  Therefore the DISTRO_VERSION is not set correct. This will be corrected
  with PD24.1.1. Please update to the newer release.
  No functional issue.
